    {
      "sentence_id": 13,
      "text": "Learned State as well as learned counsel for respondent No.2 have not disputed the factum of compromise between the parties.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1620,
      "end": 1744,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 14,
      "text": "In view of the above, no useful purpose would be served to continue with the proceedings before the trial Court in the instant F.I.R.\nFollowing the principles laid down by the Full Bench judgment of this Court in Kulwinder Singh and others Versus State of Punjab and another 2007 (3) RCR (Criminal) 1052 and approved by the Hon'ble Supreme Court in Gian Singh Versus State of Punjab and others (2012) 10 SCC 303, this petition is allowed and F.I.R. No.88 dated 11.07.2017 registered under Sections 420, 467, 468, 471 of the IPC, 1860 registered at Police Station Islamabad, District Amritsar and all subsequent proceedings arising therefrom on the basis of compromise dated 05.07.2021 (Annexure P-2), are quashed qua the petitioner.",
